        {
          "title": "Classes and the Object Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Class vs Instance",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==class== is a blueprint; `Dog('Rex')` creates an ==instance==",
                "Classes are objects too: instances of {purple:`type`}",
                "`__new__` **creates** the object; `__init__` only initialises it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. `__init__` and self",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`__init__(self, ...)` runs on an already-created object",
                "It must return ==None==",
                "`self` is just the first parameter, passed automatically",
                "`d.bark()` is `Dog.bark(d)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class Dog:",
                "    def __init__(self, name):",
                "        self.name = name",
                "    def bark(self): return self.name",
                "d = Dog('Rex')",
                "print(d.bark() == Dog.bark(d), type(Dog))",
                "print(d.__dict__)"
              ],
              "note": "method call = function call with the instance first"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "True <class 'type'>",
                "{'name': 'Rex'}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Where Attributes Live and Lookup",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Instance attributes: `obj.__dict__`, per object",
                "Class attributes: `Class.__dict__`, ==shared== by all instances"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Instance",
                    "sub": "`obj.__dict__`",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Class",
                    "sub": "`Class.__dict__`",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Base classes",
                    "sub": "via MRO",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "AttributeError",
                    "sub": "not found",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Instance vs Class Attributes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Instance vs Class Attributes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Shared vs per-object",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Class attribute==: in the class body, shared by all",
                "==Instance attribute==: `self.x` in `__init__`, per object",
                "Reading `d.species` falls back to the class",
                "`d.species = 'x'` creates an instance attribute that ==shadows== the class one"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class Dog:",
                "    species = 'canine'",
                "d = Dog()",
                "d.species = 'x'",
                "print(Dog.species, d.species)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "canine x"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Method kinds",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Kind",
                "Gets",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "instance method",
                  "`self`",
                  "per-object behaviour"
                ],
                [
                  "`@classmethod`",
                  "`cls`",
                  "alternative constructor, e.g. `from_json`"
                ],
                [
                  "`@staticmethod`",
                  "nothing",
                  "plain function, namespaced"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mutable traps",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`tags = []` in the class body: ==one list shared== by every instance",
                "Fix: `self.tags = []` in `__init__`",
                "`def __init__(self, items=[])`: one list shared across calls",
                "Fix: `items=None`, then `self.items = [] if items is None else items`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Assigning through an instance never edits the class; mutating a shared list does."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Does `d.x = 1` change `Dog.x`?** No, it shadows it on `d`.",
                "**Why is `items=[]` risky?** The default is built once and shared.",
                "**classmethod vs staticmethod?** `cls` is passed vs nothing."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Inheritance, MRO and super()",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Inheritance, MRO and super()",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Inheriting",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`class Child(Parent):` gets all Parent attributes and methods",
                "==Override== a method by redefining it in Child",
                "`isinstance(c, Parent)` is {green:True} for a Child instance"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. MRO and the diamond",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==MRO== = method search order, built by **C3 linearisation**",
                "View it: `D.__mro__` or `D.mro()`",
                "`class D(B, C)`, B and C both subclass A: A appears **once**, after both"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "D",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "B",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "C",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "A",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "object",
                    "ink": "black"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. super() and mistakes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`super()` follows the MRO of ==type(self)==, not just the parent",
                "So in B, `super()` can reach **C**, the next class in line"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "class A:",
                "    def hi(self): print(\"A\")",
                "class B(A):",
                "    def hi(self): print(\"B\"); super().hi()",
                "class C(A):",
                "    def hi(self): print(\"C\"); super().hi()",
                "class D(B, C): pass",
                "D().hi()"
              ],
              "note": "B's super() calls C, not A"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "B",
                "C",
                "A"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Forgot `super().__init__(...)`",
              "text": "The parent `__init__` never runs, so its attributes are unset: ==AttributeError== later."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Dunder Methods and Properties",
